---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const ld = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'AboutPage', url: new URL('/about/', SITE.domain).href, mainEntity: { '@type': 'Organization', '@id': SITE.domain + '/#org', name: SITE.siteName, url: SITE.domain, email: SITE.contactEmail, founder: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.editorName, url: new URL('/author/muhammet-ali-turk/', SITE.domain).href } } }];
---
<Page title="About FBA Tactics" description="Who publishes FBA Tactics, what it covers, how every figure is sourced and checked, how pages are produced, and how the site is funded." kicker="About" photo="hub-about" lede="An independent reference for people who import goods into the United States and sell them on online marketplaces." jsonld={ld}>
  <h2 id="who">Who publishes the site</h2>
  <p>FBA Tactics is published and edited by <a href="/author/muhammet-ali-turk/"><strong>{SITE.editorName}</strong></a>, {SITE.publisherLocation}. Before editing the site he worked as an e-commerce specialist at Parknes Inc., a US-based e-commerce and third-party logistics company, handling listings, logistics tracking and product and competitor analysis for Amazon, Walmart and eBay sales (August 2024 – May 2025), and founded and ran a small e-commerce business, HR Express (January 2025 – January 2026). He holds a degree in Management Information Systems from Ostim Technical University. His full background is on the <a href="/author/muhammet-ali-turk/">editor page</a>. Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  <h2>What the site covers — and why the name</h2>
  <p>The name comes from the site's start as a guide for sellers using Fulfillment by Amazon. Today it covers the two things that decide whether an imported product makes money on any marketplace: what the platform charges on each sale, and what US import rules require before the goods can be sold. That means fee and terms references for Amazon, Walmart, eBay, Etsy, Shopify, TikTok Shop and AliExpress; Amazon selling operations — inventory, fulfillment programs, listings and account health; guides on entry, bonds, classification, origin, valuation, additional duties, drawback and foreign-trade zones; product compliance; and the accounting and tax that follow.</p>
  <h2>Where the facts come from</h2>
  <p>Only from the body that sets the rule or the fee: the Code of Federal Regulations, Federal Register notices, public laws, IRS publications, and each marketplace's own public fee pages. Every fact carries a numbered link to its source and the date it was checked. Blogs, forums and other summaries are not cited; software vendors are cited only for their own product and price in the seller software section, and a figure that cannot be traced to a source a reader can open is not published. The rules are set out on <a href="/editorial-standards/">how we check facts</a>.</p>
  <h2>How pages are produced</h2>
  <p>Pages are researched and drafted with the help of AI writing tools working from the primary sources listed on each page. Every factual statement is recorded in a claims register; a separate, automated checking pass reopens each source and compares it with the sentence it supports, and anything the source does not support is corrected or removed. Each page shows its editor, the date its facts were last verified and the full list of sources. The editor is responsible for everything published here and for correcting it.</p>
  <p>The site does not test products, software or service providers and does not rate them or publish testimonials. The pages in the <a href="/reviews/">seller software</a> section describe what each vendor officially publishes about its own product and price, and say so.</p>
  <h2>Photos and graphics</h2>
  <p>Photos are free-license images from Unsplash, used under the Unsplash License, and credited under each photo and on the <a href="/image-credits/">image credits</a> page. They illustrate a topic; they do not show the publisher, its staff or its customers. Charts and diagrams are drawn by the site from the sourced figures.</p>
  <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
  <p>The site is intended to be funded by display advertising from Google AdSense. Advertisers do not choose, review or influence content; ads are labeled and kept out of tables, calculators, navigation and source lists. There are no sponsored posts, affiliate links or paid placements; see the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate and advertising disclosure</a>.</p>
  <h2>What this site is not</h2>
  <p>It is not legal, tax or customs advice and is not affiliated with any marketplace or government agency. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</p>
</Page>
